= Entity — Simple =

An '''entity''' is something we treat as a distinct thing when we talk about or represent a system.

An entity can be:

* a person;
* an object;
* an event;
* an organization;
* a place;
* a number;
* a software system.

"Entity" is a very broad word.

An entity is not the same as its name.

The planet Venus is one entity even though people have used different names for it.

An entity is also not the same as a [[Concept/Simple|concept]]. The concept "planet" can apply to many different planetary entities.

In databases and [[Knowledge graph/Simple|knowledge graphs]], entities often receive identifiers. The identifier helps us refer to the entity, but the identifier is not the entity itself.

